{%- doc -%}
Renders a FAQ "Text + image/video" block: optional title, rich text, and up to 3 media items (image
or video, chosen per slot - video wins over image when both are set, same as Media Blocks' Carousel).
Single column (title, then text, then media) on mobile, stacked in that order; from 700px up, when
there's at least one media item, whichever of title/text/media are actually present on THIS block
share the row: title (when present) is a flat 20%, text and media split the rest 40/40 - see the
grid-template-columns rule near the end of this file for why that has to be computed per block
instead of once for the section.

The text content can optionally become a card (show_text_card): background from a Color scheme, the
section's own corner radius and the same interior padding already used elsewhere in FAQ
(.faq-content-box, assets/theme.css). Once there's media next to it, the card collapses to roughly
the media's own rendered height instead of growing past it, revealing a "Show more"/"Show less"
toggle to expand/collapse it - the same pattern (and reusing the same "Show more/less" translation
strings) as the product description on the main product page, snippets/product-info.liquid.

Every media item - whether there's one or several - renders through the exact same shared markup as
Media Blocks' Carousel: snippets/media-zoom-slide.liquid (sound/play-pause toggle, zoom-to-lightbox),
snippets/media-lightbox.liquid, snippets/media-zoom-script.liquid and snippets/media-zoom-style.liquid.
With more than one media item, they additionally scroll inside a <product-list> exactly like
sections/media-blocks.liquid's 'carousel' block cells do - see that section for the other caller of
the same snippets. Each item's caption (its own per-slide caption) is drawn INSIDE the photo/video, in white, aligned to the left,
at the bottom edge with no background or shadow - like the gallery on the main product page.
There's no separate caption strip/slider.

@param {object} block - the "text_image" block to render
@param {number} [fit_from] - width in px from which the media sits next to the text, where the gallery fits the height of the text card (default 700)
@param {number} [faq_border_radius] - the section's own corner radius (Corner radius setting), applied to the media (and the text card, when enabled) so they match the section's rounded corners
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign slide_count = 0
  assign single_slide_image = nil
  assign single_slide_video = nil
  assign single_slide_caption = nil
  assign single_slide_show_icon = false
  assign single_slide_icon_type = nil
  assign single_slide_icon_size = nil
  assign single_slide_icon_spin = nil
  assign single_slide_icon_primary_color = nil
  assign single_slide_icon_secondary_color = nil
  assign single_slide_icon_border_color = nil
  assign single_ring_style = nil

  for i in (1..3)
    assign image_key = 'image_' | append: i
    assign video_key = 'video_' | append: i
    assign caption_key = 'caption_' | append: i
    assign slide_show_icon_key = 'show_icon_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_type_key = 'icon_type_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_size_key = 'icon_size_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_spin_key = 'icon_spin_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_primary_color_key = 'icon_primary_color_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_secondary_color_key = 'icon_secondary_color_' | append: i
    assign slide_icon_border_color_key = 'icon_border_color_' | append: i
    assign slide_ring_key = 'show_ring_' | append: i
    assign ring_x_key = 'ring_x_' | append: i
    assign ring_y_key = 'ring_y_' | append: i
    assign ring_size_key = 'ring_size_' | append: i
    assign slide_ring_style = nil

    if block.settings[slide_ring_key]
      assign slide_ring_style = '--ring-x: ' | append: block.settings[ring_x_key] | append: '%; --ring-y: ' | append: block.settings[ring_y_key] | append: '%; --ring-size: ' | append: block.settings[ring_size_key] | append: '%;'
    endif

    if block.settings[image_key] != blank or block.settings[video_key] != blank
      assign slide_count = slide_count | plus: 1

      # Only meaningful when slide_count ends up at exactly 1 (the non-carousel path below) - picks
      # up whichever slot actually has content, instead of assuming it's always "Media 1" (a single
      # photo/video can be placed in any of the 3 slots, not just the first one).
      if single_slide_image == nil and single_slide_video == nil
        assign single_slide_image = block.settings[image_key]
        assign single_slide_video = block.settings[video_key]
        assign single_slide_caption = block.settings[caption_key]
        assign single_slide_show_icon = block.settings[slide_show_icon_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_type = block.settings[slide_icon_type_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_size = block.settings[slide_icon_size_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_spin = block.settings[slide_icon_spin_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_primary_color = block.settings[slide_icon_primary_color_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_secondary_color = block.settings[slide_icon_secondary_color_key]
        assign single_slide_icon_border_color = block.settings[slide_icon_border_color_key]
        assign single_ring_style = slide_ring_style
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign has_media = false

  if slide_count > 0
    assign has_media = true
  endif

  assign is_carousel = false

  if slide_count > 1
    assign is_carousel = true
  endif


  assign has_title_column = false

  if block.settings.title != blank or block.settings.show_icon
    assign has_title_column = true
  endif

  assign has_text_column = false

  if block.settings.text != blank
    assign has_text_column = true
  endif

  # Needed early (not just down by the media markup) since the text card, when it's set to match the
  # media's height, has to know this element's id too - see read-more-match-height further down.
  assign media_wrapper_id = 'faq-text-image-media-' | append: block.id

  # Icon row layout (title + decorative icon): plain flex, not grid - a grid with a "1fr" track only
  # behaves predictably when the row itself has a definite width to distribute, which isn't the case
  # here (the title column below is a flat 20% of the row, never stretched). Flex sizes both the
  # title and the icon to their own content regardless, so "Left"/"Right" never has odd/inconsistent
  # sizing. "icon_alignment" (left/center/right) only has visible room to act on "Above"/"Below" (a
  # flex column, where the title and icon can differ in width) - for "Left"/"Right" the row is
  # exactly as wide as title + icon + gap, so there's no extra space left to align within.
  assign icon_flex_direction = 'row'

  case block.settings.icon_position
    when 'left'
      assign icon_flex_direction = 'row-reverse'
    when 'above'
      assign icon_flex_direction = 'column-reverse'
    when 'below'
      assign icon_flex_direction = 'column'
  endcase

  assign icon_is_column = false

  if icon_flex_direction == 'column' or icon_flex_direction == 'column-reverse'
    assign icon_is_column = true
  endif

  assign icon_justify_self = 'flex-start'

  case block.settings.icon_alignment
    when 'center'
      assign icon_justify_self = 'center'
    when 'right'
      assign icon_justify_self = 'flex-end'
  endcase

  assign heading_row_id = 'faq-text-image-heading-row-' | append: block.id
  assign text_image_id = 'faq-text-image-' | append: block.id
  assign border_radius_px = faq_border_radius | default: 0 | append: 'px'
-%}

{%- if block.settings.title != blank or block.settings.text != blank or block.settings.show_icon or has_media -%}
  <div class="faq__text-image {% if has_media %}faq__text-image--with-image{% endif %}" id="{{ text_image_id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- if has_title_column -%}
      <div class="faq__text-image-title prose">
        <div class="faq__text-image-heading-row" id="{{ heading_row_id }}">
          {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
            <div class="faq__text-image-heading-row__title">
              {%- render 'heading', content: block.settings.title, style: block.settings.title_tag, html_tag: 'h3', balance_text: true -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if block.settings.show_icon -%}
            <div class="faq__text-image-heading-row__icon">
              {%- render 'decorative-icon',
                icon_type: block.settings.icon_type,
                icon_size: block.settings.icon_size,
                icon_spin: block.settings.icon_spin,
                icon_primary_color: block.settings.icon_primary_color,
                icon_secondary_color: block.settings.icon_secondary_color,
                icon_border_color: block.settings.icon_border_color
              -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <style>
        {%- comment -%}
        Same two-levels-deep .prose spacing fix as contact.liquid's .contact-heading-row__title - see
        that section for the full rationale (the heading sits past .prose's own one-level exemption).
        Unconditional (not only when show_icon): the extra wrapping div this fix targets
        (.faq__text-image-heading-row__title) exists whenever the title itself renders, with or
        without an icon next to it - gating this on show_icon left the title's own top margin
        unreset, and so pushed down, whenever the icon was off.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
          #{{ heading_row_id }} .faq__text-image-heading-row__title > * {
            text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic;
            margin-block-start: 0;
          }
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if block.settings.show_icon -%}
          #{{ heading_row_id }} {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: {{ icon_flex_direction }};
            align-items: {% if icon_is_column %}flex-start{% else %}center{% endif %};
            gap: .5rem;
          }

          {%- if icon_is_column -%}
            #{{ heading_row_id }} .faq__text-image-heading-row__icon {
              align-self: {{ icon_justify_self }};
            }
          {%- endif -%}

          #{{ heading_row_id }} .faq__text-image-heading-row__icon svg {
            margin-block: calc(var(--prose-media-spacing) / 2);
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      </style>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if has_text_column -%}
      {%- assign text_card_matches_media = false -%}

      {%- if block.settings.show_text_card and has_media -%}
        {%- assign text_card_matches_media = true -%}
        {%- assign text_content_id = 'faq-text-image-text-content-' | append: block.id -%}

        {%- comment -%}
        Same "collapse + Show more/less" pattern as the product description on the main product page
        (snippets/product-info.liquid's <read-more-text>, "Show more/less" comment) - reused here as a
        distinct custom element (read-more-match-height, not read-more-text) because its "how tall
        should the collapsed state be" rule is different: product-info.liquid clamps to a fixed number
        of lines; this instead matches whatever height the media/carousel next to it actually renders
        at (measured in JS, not assumed - works the same regardless of block_size/mobile_block_size,
        including "Original image ratio", and on every breakpoint, carousel or single item alike).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <read-more-match-height
          class="faq__text-image-text faq-content-box faq__text-image-text--card color-scheme color-scheme--{{ block.settings.text_card_color_scheme.id }}"
          style="border-radius: {{ border_radius_px }};"
          data-match-id="{{ media_wrapper_id }}"
        >
          <div id="{{ text_content_id }}" class="prose faq__text-image-text-content" data-min-lines="2">
            {{- block.settings.text -}}
          </div>

          <button type="button" class="link faq__text-image-text-toggle" aria-controls="{{ text_content_id }}">
            <span class="faq__text-image-text-toggle__label-more">{{ 'product.general.show_more' | t }}</span><span class="faq__text-image-text-toggle__label-less">{{ 'product.general.show_less' | t }}</span>
          </button>
        </read-more-match-height>

        <script>
          function fitToLine(content, target) {
            // Largest bottom edge (from the top of content) of any text line / media that still fits inside
            // target, so the collapsed box ends right under a whole line - never through the middle of one.
            // Text rects include the descenders, and the +2px keeps ascenders/descenders from being shaved.
            var top = content.getBoundingClientRect().top;
            var best = 0;
            var range = document.createRange();
            var walker = document.createTreeWalker(content, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);
          
            while (walker.nextNode()) {
              if (!walker.currentNode.nodeValue.trim()) continue;
              range.selectNodeContents(walker.currentNode);
              Array.prototype.forEach.call(range.getClientRects(), function (rect) {
                var bottom = rect.bottom - top;
                if (rect.height > 0 && bottom <= target + 0.5 && bottom > best) best = bottom;
              });
            }
          
            content.querySelectorAll('img, svg, video').forEach(function (el) {
              var bottom = el.getBoundingClientRect().bottom - top;
              if (bottom <= target + 0.5 && bottom > best) best = bottom;
            });
          
            return best > 0 ? Math.ceil(best) + 2 : target;
          }
          
if (!window.customElements.get('read-more-match-height')) {
            window.customElements.define('read-more-match-height', class extends HTMLElement {
              connectedCallback() {
                // Deferred one frame on purpose: this element renders BEFORE the media/carousel
                // further down in the markup, so looking up data-match-id synchronously here (at
                // parse time) would run before that element even exists in the DOM yet, silently
                // finding nothing. By the next animation frame, the whole page has been parsed.
                requestAnimationFrame(this.init.bind(this));
              }

              init() {
                var content = this.querySelector('.faq__text-image-text-content');
                var toggle = this.querySelector('.faq__text-image-text-toggle');
                var matchTarget = this.dataset.matchId ? document.getElementById(this.dataset.matchId) : null;
                if (!content || !toggle || !matchTarget) return;

                this.content = content;
                this.toggle = toggle;
                this.matchTarget = matchTarget;

                toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                toggle.addEventListener('click', this.onToggleClick.bind(this));

                this.measure();

                // The glued bar of the FAQ (sections/faq.liquid) changes how much of the gallery's height belongs to the card
                this.onBarResize = this.measure.bind(this);
                window.addEventListener('faq-bar-resize', this.onBarResize);

                if (window.ResizeObserver) {
                  // Both: matchTarget resizing (eg. the carousel changing height on a breakpoint
                  // change, or an "Original image ratio" photo finishing load) and content resizing
                  // (eg. a webfont swap reflowing the text) can each change whether this should be
                  // collapsed/overflowing, independently of the other.
                  this.resizeObserver = new ResizeObserver(this.measure.bind(this));
                  this.resizeObserver.observe(matchTarget);
                  this.resizeObserver.observe(content);
                }
              }

              disconnectedCallback() {
                if (this.resizeObserver) this.resizeObserver.disconnect();
                if (this.onBarResize) window.removeEventListener('faq-bar-resize', this.onBarResize);
              }

              // With the FAQ's glued bar, the gallery of the first block of the open category rises to the top of the bar (sections/faq.liquid),
              // so the white container is the bar plus this card, and the card is that much shorter than the gallery. Zero anywhere else.
              barHeight() {
                var block = this.closest('.faq__text-image');
                if (!block || block.parentElement.firstElementChild !== block || !block.parentElement.classList.contains('faq__panel')) return 0;
                return parseFloat(getComputedStyle(this).getPropertyValue('--faq-bar-height')) || 0;
              }

              // True while the media sits next to the card (two or more grid columns).
              mediaIsBeside() {
                var block = this.closest('.faq__text-image');
                return !!block && getComputedStyle(block).gridTemplateColumns.trim().split(/\s+/).length > 1;
              }

              // The gallery's own height (what its size setting asks for), not the one it is fitted to: next to the card the gallery is fitted to the
              // card's height (see the "fit" rules in the style block of this snippet), so for a moment the fit is switched off (data-natural), the
              // height read, and the fit switched back on - all synchronous, nothing is painted in between. That natural height is the limit of the card.
              naturalMediaHeight() {
                var block = this.closest('.faq__text-image');
                if (!block || !this.mediaIsBeside()) return this.matchTarget.offsetHeight;

                block.setAttribute('data-natural', '');
                var height = this.matchTarget.offsetHeight;
                block.removeAttribute('data-natural');
                return height;
              }

              // While the card is open ("Show more") the gallery keeps the height it had with the card closed: only the card grows.
              pinGallery() {
                var block = this.closest('.faq__text-image');
                if (!block) return;
                block.style.setProperty('--faq-gallery-height', (this.collapsedHeight + this.chromeHeight + this.barHeight()) + 'px');
              }

              measure() {
                // matchTarget.offsetHeight is the TOTAL card's target height, but collapsedHeight
                // below clamps only the inner .faq__text-image-text-content - so this card's own
                // padding (.faq-content-box) and the toggle's own space (shown or not) both have to
                // be subtracted first, or the card would end up that much taller than the carousel
                // instead of matching it. The toggle is measured by briefly forcing it visible (a
                // hidden, display: none element always reports 0 for its height) - synchronous, so
                // nothing is ever actually painted in that intermediate state.
                var cardStyle = getComputedStyle(this);
                var paddingY = parseFloat(cardStyle.paddingTop) + parseFloat(cardStyle.paddingBottom);

                this.toggle.style.display = 'block';
                var toggleSpace = this.toggle.offsetHeight + parseFloat(getComputedStyle(this.toggle).marginBlockStart);
                this.toggle.style.display = '';
                this.chromeHeight = paddingY + toggleSpace;

                // Floor (data-min-lines, same --text-line-height token product-info.liquid's own
                // line-based collapse uses): a short enough carousel could otherwise leave nothing of
                // the text actually visible (collapsedHeight clamped to 0 by the line below) - a
                // couple of lines always showing is a stronger hint there's a "Show more" to reveal
                // than an empty box would be.
                var minLines = parseFloat(this.content.dataset.minLines) || 0;
                var lineHeight = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(this.content).lineHeight) || 0;
                var minHeight = minLines * lineHeight;

                this.collapsedHeight = Math.max(minHeight, this.naturalMediaHeight() - this.barHeight() - paddingY - toggleSpace);

                // Moved up to the bottom of the last whole line that fits (measured, so paragraph
                // spacing is accounted for) - the collapsed box never ends in the middle of a line.
                // Only when the text really is longer than the limit: text that fits entirely must not be cut to its last line (short texts).
                if (this.content.scrollHeight - this.collapsedHeight > 1) {
                  this.collapsedHeight = Math.max(fitToLine(this.content, this.collapsedHeight), minHeight);
                }

                if (this.hasAttribute('data-expanded')) {
                  // Keeps the open height in sync with a resize instead of leaving it pinned to
                  // whatever it measured when it was expanded.
                  this.content.style.maxHeight = this.content.scrollHeight + 'px';
                  this.pinGallery();
                  return;
                }

                var overflowing = this.content.scrollHeight - this.collapsedHeight > 1;
                this.toggleAttribute('data-overflowing', overflowing);
                this.content.style.maxHeight = overflowing ? this.collapsedHeight + 'px' : '';
              }

              onToggleClick() {
                var expanding = !this.hasAttribute('data-expanded');

                if (expanding) {
                  this.pinGallery();
                  this.content.style.maxHeight = this.content.scrollHeight + 'px';
                  this.setAttribute('data-expanded', '');
                } else {
                  this.removeAttribute('data-expanded');
                  this.content.style.maxHeight = this.collapsedHeight + 'px';
                }

                this.toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(expanding));
              }
            });
          }
        </script>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless text_card_matches_media -%}
        {%- comment -%}
        .prose sits one level deeper here (its own .faq__text-image-text-content div, not directly on
        .faq__text-image-text) to match the read-more-match-height case above exactly - that one NEEDS
        the extra level (the clamped content has to be a separate element from the card and its toggle
        button), so keeping both paths the same depth means .prose's own nesting-depth-sensitive rules
        (eg. the heading margin fix above) behave identically regardless of which path rendered.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="faq__text-image-text {% if block.settings.show_text_card %}faq-content-box faq__text-image-text--card color-scheme color-scheme--{{ block.settings.text_card_color_scheme.id }}{% endif %}" {% if block.settings.show_text_card %}style="border-radius: {{ border_radius_px }};"{% endif %}>
          <div class="prose faq__text-image-text-content">
            {{- block.settings.text -}}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if has_media -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign media_corner_radius = border_radius_px
        assign media_lightbox_id = 'faq-text-image-lightbox-' | append: block.id
        assign media_carousel_id = nil

        if is_carousel
          assign media_carousel_id = 'faq-text-image-carousel-' | append: block.id
        endif
      -%}

      <div class="faq__text-image-media" id="{{ media_wrapper_id }}">
        {%- if is_carousel -%}
          {%- comment -%}
          border-radius lives directly on <product-list> itself (CSS below, next to its existing
          grid rule) - same technique as sections/instagram-feed.liquid's .instagram-feed__carousel:
          the SAME element that already has overflow-x: auto / overflow-y: hidden (.scroll-area)
          also gets the rounded corners, so the clip stays correctly tied to its own scrollport as
          it scrolls. Each slide's caption lives inside its own slide frame (see below), so it scrolls
          with its photo and needs no separate, synced element.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <product-list id="{{ media_carousel_id }}" cell-selector=".snap-start" class="scroll-area snap-x">
              {%- liquid
                assign lightbox_slide_index = 0
              -%}
              {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
                {%- capture image_key -%}image_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture video_key -%}video_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture caption_key -%}caption_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture ring_key -%}show_ring_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture ring_x_key -%}ring_x_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture ring_y_key -%}ring_y_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture ring_size_key -%}ring_size_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture show_icon_key -%}show_icon_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_type_key -%}icon_type_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_size_key -%}icon_size_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_spin_key -%}icon_spin_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_primary_color_key -%}icon_primary_color_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_secondary_color_key -%}icon_secondary_color_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- capture icon_border_color_key -%}icon_border_color_{{ i }}{%- endcapture -%}

                {%- assign slide_image = block.settings[image_key] -%}
                {%- assign slide_video = block.settings[video_key] -%}
                {%- assign slide_show_icon = block.settings[show_icon_key] -%}

                {%- if slide_image != blank or slide_video != blank -%}
                  {%- assign slide_caption = block.settings[caption_key] -%}
                  {%- assign slide_caption_id = media_wrapper_id | append: '-caption-' | append: i -%}

                  <div class="snap-start faq__text-image-media-frame"{% if slide_caption != blank %} aria-describedby="{{ slide_caption_id }}"{% endif %}>
                    {%- render 'media-zoom-slide',
                      video: slide_video,
                      image: slide_image,
                      block_size: block.settings.block_size,
                      mobile_block_size: block.settings.mobile_block_size,
                      corner_radius: media_corner_radius,
                      lightbox_id: media_lightbox_id,
                      aria_controls_id: media_carousel_id,
                      lightbox_index: lightbox_slide_index,
                      enable_lightbox: false,
                      sizes: '(max-width: 699px) 100vw, 33vw'
                    -%}

                    {%- if slide_show_icon -%}
                      <div class="faq__text-image-slide-icon">
                        {%- render 'decorative-icon',
                          icon_type: block.settings[icon_type_key],
                          icon_size: block.settings[icon_size_key],
                          icon_spin: block.settings[icon_spin_key],
                          icon_primary_color: block.settings[icon_primary_color_key],
                          icon_secondary_color: block.settings[icon_secondary_color_key],
                          icon_border_color: block.settings[icon_border_color_key]
                        -%}
                      </div>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {%- if block.settings[ring_key] -%}
                      <div class="faq__text-image-ring" style="--ring-x: {{ block.settings[ring_x_key] }}%; --ring-y: {{ block.settings[ring_y_key] }}%; --ring-size: {{ block.settings[ring_size_key] }}%;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {%- if slide_caption != blank -%}
                      <figcaption class="faq__text-image-caption" id="{{ slide_caption_id }}">{{ slide_caption }}</figcaption>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>

                  {%- assign lightbox_slide_index = lightbox_slide_index | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </product-list>

          {%- comment -%}Dots under the carousel (snippets/carousel-dots.liquid), the navigation on every screen size{%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'carousel-dots', target_id: media_carousel_id -%}

          {%- render 'media-lightbox', id: media_lightbox_id, show_nav: true -%}

        {%- else -%}
          <figure>
            <div class="faq__text-image-media-frame">
              {%- render 'media-zoom-slide',
                video: single_slide_video,
                image: single_slide_image,
                block_size: block.settings.block_size,
                mobile_block_size: block.settings.mobile_block_size,
                corner_radius: media_corner_radius,
                lightbox_id: media_lightbox_id,
                lightbox_index: 0,
                as_lightbox_cell: true,
                enable_lightbox: false,
                sizes: '(max-width: 699px) 100vw, 33vw'
              -%}

              {%- if single_slide_show_icon -%}
                <div class="faq__text-image-slide-icon">
                  {%- render 'decorative-icon',
                    icon_type: single_slide_icon_type,
                    icon_size: single_slide_icon_size,
                    icon_spin: single_slide_icon_spin,
                    icon_primary_color: single_slide_icon_primary_color,
                    icon_secondary_color: single_slide_icon_secondary_color,
                    icon_border_color: single_slide_icon_border_color
                  -%}
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if single_ring_style != blank -%}
                <div class="faq__text-image-ring" style="{{ single_ring_style }}" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if single_slide_caption != blank -%}
                <figcaption class="faq__text-image-caption">{{ single_slide_caption }}</figcaption>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </figure>

          {%- render 'media-lightbox', id: media_lightbox_id, show_nav: false -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <style>
        {%- comment -%}
        Per-slide decorative icon (block.settings.show_icon_1/2/3): a badge floating over the
        top-left corner of that slide's photo/video, same icon system as the title's own (just a
        separate, independent type/size/color config per slide - see sections/faq.liquid's schema).
        Top-LEFT, not top-right: media-zoom-style.liquid positions a video's own sound/play-pause
        controls at the top-right of every slide (.carousel-video-controls, inset-inline-end: 1rem) -
        top-left is the one corner never used by anything else this block renders, on image or video
        slides alike, so the icon can't ever sit on top of those buttons.

        .faq__text-image-media-frame (position: relative + overflow: hidden, wrapping the media, the
        icon and the caption together) keeps them clipped to the media's own box, with the same
        rounded corners as the media - without it, a large icon (up to 80px) over a short "Original
        image ratio" photo could spill past the photo's bottom edge.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-media-frame {
          position: relative;
          overflow: hidden;
          border-radius: {{ media_corner_radius }};
        }

        {%- comment -%}
        Caption inside the photo/video, like the gallery of the main product page: white text aligned to the left at the
        bottom edge with no background or shadow, at the bottom edge of the photo, inset by the theme's --container-gutter on the left, right and bottom (the same inner padding used everywhere else). pointer-events: none so
        the caption never blocks the zoom / play buttons under it. Overrides theme.css's global
        figcaption { margin-block-start: .625rem !important; } for this caption only.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
        Spinning circle (show_ring_N): a white dashed circle centered on a point of the photo (--ring-x / --ring-y, in % of the
        photo) with a width of --ring-size % of the photo, to point out an area (eg. a wrinkle). Only the dashed line turns (the
        ::before), the box itself stays put so the position never drifts. Under the caption, over the photo; it never blocks clicks.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-ring {
          position: absolute;
          left: var(--ring-x);
          top: var(--ring-y);
          width: var(--ring-size);
          aspect-ratio: 1;
          translate: -50% -50%;
          z-index: 1;
          pointer-events: none;
        }

        #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-ring::before {
          content: "";
          position: absolute;
          inset: 0;
          border: 1px dashed #fff;
          border-radius: 50%;
          animation: faq-ring-spin 24s linear infinite;
        }

        @keyframes faq-ring-spin {
          to { rotate: 360deg; }
        }

        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
          #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-ring::before {
            animation: none;
          }
        }

        #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-caption {
          position: absolute;
          inset-inline: 0;
          inset-block-end: 0;
          z-index: 1;
          margin: 0 !important;
          padding: 0 var(--container-gutter) var(--container-gutter);
          line-height: 1.25;
          color: #fff;
          text-align: start;
          pointer-events: none;
        }

        #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .faq__text-image-slide-icon {
          top: .75rem;
          left: .75rem;
          z-index: 2;
          position: absolute;
          pointer-events: none;
        }

        {%- if is_carousel -%}
          {%- comment -%}
          Flexbox, not a percentage-width grid: every slide shares one flex-basis (85% on mobile,
          45% from 700px up - the same reference width Media Blocks' Carousel uses) and the same
          flex-grow (1) and flex-shrink (0). That one rule handles both slide counts this block can
          actually have on its own, without special-casing either:

          - 2 slides (2 * 45% = 90%, fits): flex-grow distributes the 10% of leftover space between
          them EQUALLY (same grow factor on both), so they end up the same width as each other,
          filling the row exactly - no gap left over.
          - 3 slides (3 * 45% = 135%, doesn't fit): flex-shrink: 0 forbids shrinking below that 45%
          basis to make room, so the row overflows instead and scrolls - all three stay the same
          width as each other and as a 2-slide row's own 45% (nothing stretches just because a 3rd
          slide happens to be present).

          align-items: start (flex's own default is stretch) keeps each media cell at its own
          natural height instead of being stretched to match the row's tallest slide - with
          block_size "auto" ("Original image ratio"), stretching would otherwise distort that
          slide's aspect ratio to fill a taller row.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          #{{ media_carousel_id }} {
            display: flex;
            align-items: start;
            gap: var(--horizontal-gap);
          }

          {%- comment -%}
          The gap between the media items is the theme's shared carousel gap (--horizontal-gap, css-variables.liquid), the same one the Instagram feed
          uses, on mobile and on desktop.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
            #{{ media_carousel_id }} {
              column-gap: var(--horizontal-gap);
            }
          }

          {%- comment -%}
          The carousel's own cells are <div class="snap-start faq__text-image-media-frame">.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          #{{ media_carousel_id }} > .snap-start {
            flex: 1 0 85%;
            min-width: 0;
          }

          @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
            #{{ media_carousel_id }} > .snap-start {
              flex-basis: 45%;
            }
          }

          #{{ media_carousel_id }} {
            border-radius: {{ media_corner_radius }};
          }

          {%- comment -%}
          theme.css's .snap-start also sets scroll-snap-stop: always, which makes the carousel stop at every
          single slide: a fast swipe can never travel over more than one, which feels stiff on a row where
          several slides are visible at once. normal lets a fling glide over slides and settle on the nearest
          snap point (the snap itself, x mandatory, is unchanged).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          #{{ media_carousel_id }} > .snap-start {
            scroll-snap-stop: normal;
          }

        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
        The "Small" size of this block is taller than the theme's own min-h-sm (assets/theme.css, shared with other sections - which keep theirs): about
        halfway between the theme's Small and Medium. Phones (up to 999px) read the Mobile block size, from 1000px the Block size; scoped to this block
        (the id) and to its own breakpoints so the other sizes keep winning where they apply.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        @media screen and (max-width: 999px) {
          #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .content-box.min-h-sm {
            min-height: clamp(17.5rem, 40vmax, 30rem);
          }
        }

        @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
          #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .content-box.md\:min-h-sm {
            min-height: clamp(17.5rem, 45vmax, 30rem);
          }
        }

        {%- if block.settings.block_size == 'auto' -%}
          {%- comment -%}
          theme.css's own desktop (1000px+) rule that makes a sized media item's background fill its
          content-box via position: absolute (".content-box[class*='md:min-h-'] .content-box__background-media")
          matches ANY "md:min-h-*" class, including "md:min-h-auto" - unlike its mobile equivalent
          (".content-box[class*='min-h-']:not(.min-h-auto) ..."), which correctly excludes the "auto"
          ("Original image ratio") case. With no sized min-height class to size against and its own
          media pulled out of flow, an "auto"-sized content-box has nothing left to size itself from at
          1000px+, collapsing the figure around it (and with it the caption drawn over the photo). This restores the same static positioning
          theme.css's own mobile rule already uses for "auto", scoped to this block only.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
            #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .content-box__background-media {
              position: static;
              inset: auto;
            }
          }
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if has_text_column -%}
          #{{ text_image_id }}[data-natural] #{{ media_wrapper_id }} {
            align-self: start;
          }

          {%- comment -%}
          Gallery takes the height of the text (the white card) next to them, never the other way round. From 700px, when the media sits
          beside the text: contain: size makes the media column add nothing to the row's height (the row is as tall as the card), and the
          column then stretches to that height (align-self) as a flex column - the photos/videos (carousel + dots) take that height
          (flex: 1 1 0). Photos fill their box (object-fit: cover, the "image-cover" class).
          Phones keep the stacked layout, and so does any width where the section stacks the block (fit_from).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          @media screen and (min-width: {{ fit_from | default: 700 }}px) {
            #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} {
              contain: size;
              align-self: stretch;
              display: flex;
              flex-direction: column;
              min-height: 0;
            }

            #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .content-box {
              height: 100%;
              min-height: 0;
            }

            #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .content-box > .content-box__background-media {
              position: absolute;
              inset: 0;
            }

            {%- if is_carousel -%}
              #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_carousel_id }} {
                flex: 1 1 0;
                min-height: 6rem;
                align-items: stretch;
              }

              #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_carousel_id }} > .snap-start {
                height: 100%;
              }

              #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_carousel_id }}-dots {
                flex: none;
              }
            {%- else -%}
              #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} > figure {
                flex: 1 1 0;
                min-height: 0;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
              }

              #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} > figure > .faq__text-image-media-frame {
                flex: 1 1 0;
                min-height: 6rem;
              }
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}"Show more" open: the gallery keeps the height it had with the card closed (--faq-gallery-height, set by the script above), only the card grows.{%- endcomment -%}
            #{{ text_image_id }}:not([data-natural]):has(read-more-match-height[data-expanded]) #{{ media_wrapper_id }} {
              align-self: start;
              height: var(--faq-gallery-height);
            }
          }
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'media-zoom-style',
          wrapper_id: media_wrapper_id,
          lightbox_id: media_lightbox_id,
          corner_radius: media_corner_radius,
          has_multiple_slides: is_carousel
        -%}

        {%- comment -%}
        Desktop (1000px and up): the logo drawn on the video thumbnails (media-zoom-style.liquid, 3.5rem x 2rem) is a bit larger, 4.25rem x 2.45rem, the same as in
        the Instagram feed; its inset stays at .75rem. Not for the expanded video in the lightbox, which has its own size.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
          #{{ media_wrapper_id }} .has-video-logo video-media:not(.is-lightbox-expanded)::after {
            width: min(4.25rem, 28%);
            height: 2.45rem;
          }
        }
      </style>

      {%- render 'media-zoom-script', wrapper_id: media_wrapper_id, lightbox_id: media_lightbox_id, carousel_id: media_carousel_id -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if has_media -%}
    <style>
      {%- comment -%}
      Desktop column widths, computed for THIS block specifically: a section-wide rule can't do this,
      since which of title/text/media are actually present varies block by block. With no title, for
      example, the row splits 50/50 between text and media instead of leaving an empty title column
      and media stuck sharing only 1 of 3 tracks. The title column, when present, is a flat 20% (not
      minmax/auto - a fixed share, same every time regardless of how long or short the title text
      is), with text and media splitting the other 80% evenly between them (minmax(0, 1fr) each
      always resolves to exactly 40/40 once the title's share is fixed, rather than shifting around
      with the title's own content width).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
        #{{ text_image_id }}.faq__text-image--with-image {
          {%- if has_title_column and has_text_column -%}
            grid-template-columns: 20% minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
          {%- elsif has_title_column -%}
            grid-template-columns: 20% minmax(0, 1fr);
          {%- elsif has_text_column -%}
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
          {%- else -%}
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
          {%- endif -%}
        }
      }
    </style>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
